// input: after idr-simplify
// FILECHECK-OPTIONS: --implicit-check-not={{[^#]}}idr.closure --implicit-check-not=idr.apply
// countdown returns an action, and main applies it at once to a world, so
// idr-specialize calls a clone of countdown that takes the world.
// In the clone the apply meets the closures the body built and becomes a
// call, and the clone calls itself. No closure is left, and the
// output is fused. This is tests/idr/raise/io-loop.mlir, from Idris.
// CHECK: call @Main.countdown$raise${{[0-9]+}}(
// CHECK: func.func private @Main.countdown$raise${{[0-9]+}}({{.*}}!idr.world
// CHECK-DAG: idr.io.put_int
// CHECK-DAG: idr.constant "liftoff\0A"
